// Economy definitions, schema version 1 (PLAN.md sections 5 and 7, M3; docs/DECISIONS.md D23).
//
// placement_distance: a new building must lie within this many cells (Chebyshev distance between
//                     the nearest cells) of a building of its owner
// buildings:  id and sprite (names as in units.ron; the sprite is
//             assets/sprites/buildings/<sprite>.png), footprint width and height in cells, cost in
//             credits, build_time in ticks (20 per second), producer (the building type that
//             produces it), prerequisites (building types the player must own to queue it),
//             power produced and consumed, sell_value (credits refunded when sold, at most the
//             cost), and free_units (units that leave it when it is placed)
// units:      the production terms of the producible unit types of units.ron
// harvesters: ore capacity and ore removed per tick of the harvester unit types
// refineries: credits paid per ore unit by the refinery building types
//
// Which faction may produce what is the roster in skirmish.ron (M7): both factions share the
// construction yard, power plant, refinery, barracks, war factory, and tech center; the gun turret
// is the Vanguard's defence and the rocket tower the Meridian's. These values are balance data
// (docs/DECISIONS.md D51), used by no simulation test (invariant I10).
(
    schema_version: 1,
    placement_distance: 4,
    buildings: [
        (
            id: "construction_yard",
